      </div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Some problems are fixable.<br>Some are structural.</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">ShopWise separates what you can act on this week from what the market is doing to you.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rc-columns">
      <div class="rc-col rc-col-left">
        <div class="rc-col-heading"><span class="dot dot-green"></span> Things you control</div>
        <div class="rc-item"><div class="rc-icon green">📸</div><div><div class="rc-item-title">Google Maps photos & profile</div><div class="rc-item-desc">Profiles with 10+ photos get significantly more clicks. Adding photos costs nothing and takes an hour.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rc-item"><div class="rc-icon green">⭐</div><div><div class="rc-item-title">Review quality & response rate</div><div class="rc-item-desc">Responding to reviews improves local search ranking and signals trust to potential customers.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rc-item"><div class="rc-icon green">🍽️</div><div><div class="rc-item-title">Menu clarity & structure</div><div class="rc-item-desc">A well-organised menu with clear sections and photos reduces decision fatigue and increases average order value.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rc-item"><div class="rc-icon green">🌐</div><div><div class="rc-item-title">Website & delivery page quality</div><div class="rc-item-desc">Missing opening hours, no order button, or slow mobile load all push customers to competitors.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rc-item"><div class="rc-icon green">🎯</div><div><div class="rc-item-title">Positioning & differentiation</div><div class="rc-item-desc">A clear reason to choose you over the restaurant next door can be defined and communicated.</div></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="rc-col rc-col-right">
        <div class="rc-col-heading"><span class="dot dot-dark"></span> Things the market controls</div>
        <div class="rc-item"><div class="rc-icon neutral">📊</div><div><div class="rc-item-title">Local spending power & confidence</div><div class="rc-item-desc">Economic downturns and rising costs reduce how often people dine out. This is not something you can market your way out of.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rc-item"><div class="rc-icon neutral">🏘️</div><div><div class="rc-item-title">Number of nearby competitors</div><div class="rc-item-desc">If 14 similar restaurants are within 500m, your share of a fixed pool of customers is structurally constrained.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rc-item"><div class="rc-icon neutral">🚶</div><div><div class="rc-item-title">Area foot traffic</div><div class="rc-item-desc">Office vacancies, construction, or neighbourhood decline reduce the number of people walking past your door each day.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rc-item"><div class="rc-icon neutral">📅</div><div><div class="rc-item-title">Tourism seasonality</div><div class="rc-item-desc">Tourist-dependent areas see sharp demand swings that no amount of marketing can fully offset in low season.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rc-item"><div class="rc-icon neutral">💸</div><div><div class="rc-item-title">Rent, ingredient & energy costs</div><div class="rc-item-desc">External cost pressure squeezes margins regardless of how well you market or how good your food is.</div></div></div>
